      "content": "I'm analyzing thermal instability in a high-performance braking system. We're seeing some erratic fluctuations in the friction coefficient during sustained high-speed deceleration when using semi-metallic pads. It almost feels like the braking performance is behaving unpredictably once we hit the heat soak threshold. Can you explain the physics behind why the friction coefficient might fluctuate or \"act up\" instead of just a steady decline during these thermal spikes?",
